course: dictionary
lesson: 15797
title: Words that mean not nice
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The prefix un- at the start of a word means "not". If something is appealing, you like it or want it. So unappealing means not attractive, not nice or not interesting. «The soup had gone cold and looked very unappealing.» Nobody wants to eat cold, greasy soup, so unappealing means not nice to look at or eat.
explain: Use the words around it to check. «The job sounded dull, with long hours and no pay, so Sam found the idea unappealing.» The clues dull, long hours and no pay show that Sam did not want the job. Ask: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning, "not nice", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Unappealing can describe food, ideas, jobs or places. In writing, it is a polite way of saying "not nice". Writers often choose it when they want to sound fair and calm, rather than rude.
fact: Unappealing means not attractive, not nice or not interesting.
fact: The prefix un- means "not", so unappealing is the opposite of appealing.
fact: «Unappealing» food does not look or smell nice.
fact: Common phrases: look unappealing, an unappealing idea, an unappealing job.
fact: Unappealing is an adjective, so it describes a noun, and you can say more unappealing.
exercise: «The mushy peas looked unappealing on the cold plate.» What does unappealing mean here? | Very tasty and warm | *Not attractive or nice to eat | Loud and noisy | Shiny and new
exercise: «Nobody wanted to join the club after hearing the unappealing plan.» What does this suggest about the plan? | The plan was a surprise party | The plan was very long | The plan was for a picnic | *The plan did not sound nice or interesting
exercise: Which word means the opposite of unappealing? | Messy | Dull | Plain | *Attractive
test: «The room was dark, damp and smelly, an unappealing place to stay.» Why is the room unappealing? | Because it has bright, new windows | Because it is full of toys | Because it is very large | *Because it is dark, damp and smelly
test: «The idea of cleaning the garage sounded unappealing.» What does unappealing mean in this sentence? | *Not attractive or nice | Full of bright colour | Easy to do | Very exciting
exam: Which sentence uses unappealing correctly? | *The soggy, grey sprouts looked unappealing | The happy party was unappealing | The bright, fresh fruit looked unappealing | The cheerful song was unappealing
